{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/51720-indulge-the-new-guy","id":51720,"title":"Indulge the new guy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-17T11:18:33-08:00","id":51720,"title":"Indulge the new guy","content":"I am pretty new to changeling, but not to the WOD. That being said I still have a lot to learn.<br /> In short I LOVE the idea of changeling, but there are things that I am not sure of.<br /> The question that keeps coming to my mind is how many sets of contracts does a changeling character normally end up with by end game?<br /> This question keeps nagging at me because im not sure how powerful these guys can end up.<br /> Any insight is appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2026-mandoreblen","name":"Mandoreblen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T11:36:39-08:00","id":51743,"title":"","content":"Wildly variable, but there's an Eldritch Entitlement whose prerequisites include having a minimum total of twelve dots in Contracts, along with Wyrd 7.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T11:44:10-08:00","id":51750,"title":"","content":"Plus, the actual Contracts itself are vastly variable in potency and usefulness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T12:02:32-08:00","id":51761,"title":"","content":"12 dots? Wow. Depending on what contracts you take that can be pretty powerful...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2026-mandoreblen","name":"Mandoreblen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T12:11:59-08:00","id":51769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mandoreblen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/51720-indulge-the-new-guy?p=51761#post51761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">12 dots? Wow. Depending on what contracts you take that can be pretty powerful...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, although it is a bit easier to get there if the majority of those 12 dots are in sketchy goblin contracts. I don't think that contracts are necessarily good indicators of power for &quot;high level&quot; changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T12:55:23-08:00","id":51804,"title":"","content":"12 dots isn't that many dots.... I mean,. you could just get a lot of 1 dot sorts easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","name":"Dulahan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T14:09:46-08:00","id":51852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dulahan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/51720-indulge-the-new-guy?p=51804#post51804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">12 dots isn't that many dots.... I mean,. you could just get a lot of 1 dot sorts easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Entitlement in question is a group of immortal sorcerer-advisers who use the structure of serving their monarch as a stabilizing influence against the intoxicating effects of the power of the Wyrd. If you're suffering blackouts from the dizzying influence of a double-handful of parlor tricks I'm pretty sure you're not going to be scouted by the Office of the Vizierial Counsel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T15:24:26-08:00","id":51934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/51720-indulge-the-new-guy?p=51852#post51852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Entitlement in question is a group of immortal sorcerer-advisers who use the structure of serving their monarch as a stabilizing influence against the intoxicating effects of the power of the Wyrd. If you're suffering blackouts from the dizzying influence of a double-handful of parlor tricks I'm pretty sure you're not going to be scouted by the Office of the Vizierial Counsel.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, man. The idea of a magical (high Wyrd) mountebank tricking the Counsel into allowing him membership makes for a compelling character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T15:42:17-08:00","id":51940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firefly Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/51720-indulge-the-new-guy?p=51934#post51934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno, man. The idea of a magical (high Wyrd) mountebank tricking the Counsel into allowing him membership makes for a compelling character.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have political and magical savvy on par with people for whom those things are part of their <i>livelihoods</i> in addition to being interconnected enough with the stuff that holds the universe together that you are potentially <i>taking lethal damage from being around children</i> along with needing <i>weekly infusions of emotion</i>, but you can't manage to pick up <i>seven dots of Contracts that aren't all first dots</i> and think it's less trouble to try to <i>trick a bunch of immortals who can probably tell if you're lying</i>, you probably aren't cut out for the group's stated task of managing one's own Clarity by subordinating one's primary agency to the service of their monarch, even if one ignores the fact that the entitlement more often <i>recruits</i> than takes applicants.<br /> <br /> &quot;Discern whether what somebody says is true&quot; is a one-dot Goblin Contract with a negligible drawback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T19:46:57-08:00","id":52090,"title":"","content":"To the point of the original question about what constitutes a powerful changeling, compared to other WoD sources. I believe it is umportant to concider that changeling are much more creatures of pure magic than any other character type. Mage are next closest and they still have to enact rituals to manipilate and channel energies, while changelings simply trigger their contracts and blessings. Although, admittedly, the other PCs get more bang for their spell-like buck.<br /> So, my view is that changelings are likely to have twice as many Contracts as a Mage, Vampire, Werewolf, etc. has in their respective comparible &quot;spell&quot; slots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I also post a long form story, based on a Changeling: The Lost campaign at: <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10018173/1/Great-Fight-A-Twilight-Tommy-Tale\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.fanfiction.net/s/1001817...ght-Tommy-Tale</a><br /> I hope you will enjoy it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2020-gitariart","name":"GitariArt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T23:16:56-08:00","id":52175,"title":"","content":"If you know how to power game properly, I don't think it would be hard to pump up a Changeling who could do some fierce damage on par with the other races. I once played a fire elemental who could invoke armor of the elements fury without ever needing to touch open flame. I know that it's only a level one spell, but it was my first changeling and I only had her for 2 weeks, but she did take out 4 guys on her own.<br /> I don't actually know if this is relevant, but in my opinion, changelings can be on par with, say, vampires or werewolves if handled properly. Maybe even stronger...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1924,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1924-roanscribbles","user":"roanscribbles","date":". 01-18-2014, 02:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1924-roanscribbles","name":"roanscribbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1924_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T06:48:27-08:00","id":52338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>roanscribbles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/51720-indulge-the-new-guy?p=52175#post52175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you know how to power game properly, I don't think it would be hard to pump up a Changeling who could do some fierce damage on par with the other races. I once played a fire elemental who could invoke armor of the elements fury without ever needing to touch open flame. I know that it's only a level one spell, but it was my first changeling and I only had her for 2 weeks, but she did take out 4 guys on her own.<br /> I don't actually know if this is relevant, but in my opinion, changelings can be on par with, say, vampires or werewolves if handled properly. Maybe even stronger...</div> </div> </div> </div>I certainly agree with all of that. I just feel that changelings strengths reside in their magic-ness, thus they tend to gather more faster. Whereas a Vamp tends to just focus on stacking one or two spell effects and then using raw abilities for their primary strength, or a Promethian starts with a lot of useful merirts, which implies they are best suited to relying on those for their main strength.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I also post a long form story, based on a Changeling: The Lost campaign at: <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10018173/1/Great-Fight-A-Twilight-Tommy-Tale\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.fanfiction.net/s/1001817...ght-Tommy-Tale</a><br /> I hope you will enjoy it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2020-gitariart","name":"GitariArt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T13:53:52-08:00","id":52746,"title":"","content":"Clauses like the first Contract of Stone become rather nasty as well as Wyrd skyrockets, particularly if you have a high Wyrd Changeling taking beyond human levels of particular attributes. A Wyrd 7, Strength 7 Ogre doesn't need more than that one Contract and his Seeming blessing (and a few levels of Brawl, of course) to be punching at about the 20 dice level.<br /> <br /> Another interesting trick is combining certain Contracts with Goblin Vows. I once had a player with Contracts of the Moon (I think that's the one that inflicts Derangements and the like) and then Goblin Vows with particular conditions. A Clause or two and then a quick pledge and he could generally remove someone from a fight without having to strike a blow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T22:51:43-08:00","id":54493,"title":"","content":"I ran a changeling game that lasted about two years. Pretty cool game. Everyone enjoyed it and the characters accrued about 104 XP during the course of the game. I would definitely say that the characters were &quot;high level.&quot; One of them, a highly specialized shifty Darkling librarian Winter ninja-type, could definitely be stupidly threatening to any other supernatural splat in the nwod. He was a bit a ridiculous. However, he had only one Contract at 5 (Smoke). He had maybe like 6 other dots spread out about 4 Contracts. Instead, he focused his XP on his Wyrd, various Oaths (which do not cost XP to create), Merits and Hedgespinning. WIth the other characters, the players spent maybe 26 points out of the 104 XP on Contracts.<br /> <br /> Between Entitlements, Wyrd Evolution, Merits and Oaths ... Changelings can get ridiculously powerful. Combined with Skein Walking, Talecrafting and other minigames that you choose to use, changelings can accrue an intimidating amount of system supported power and never spend more than a quarter of their XP on Contracts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","user":"Firefly Night","date":". 01-21-2014, 02:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}